<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Béla III of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1148–1196</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Béla III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1172 to 1196. Raised at the Byzantine court as the intended heir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-i-komnenos">Manuel I Komnenos</a>, he returned to take the Hungarian throne and recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmia">Syrmia</a> after Manuel's death. A surviving list of his revenues suggests great wealth, and his reign saw the growth of written administration and probably the writing of the anonymous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta Hungarorum</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bela-iii-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Béla III of Hungary" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Márk Kálti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%A9pes_kr%C3%B3nika_-_122.oldal_-_III._B%C3%A9la_kir%C3%A1ly.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
